WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.040 --> 00:00:08.200
Assign a work order, log the time and parts, and mark it resolved with a note.

2
00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:11.310
Start from the most urgent job.

3
00:00:11.310 --> 00:00:14.860
Open it.

4
00:00:14.860 --> 00:00:20.660
Red means the agreed time has passed. Managers are told when that happens.

5
00:00:20.660 --> 00:00:28.580
Assign it to a technician, or to a contractor with a service contract.

6
00:00:28.580 --> 00:00:31.730
Choose who.

7
00:00:31.730 --> 00:00:37.770
Assign. They see it on their phone, in the office app.

8
00:00:37.770 --> 00:00:43.200
Log the time spent on the job.

9
00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:45.860
Two hours, for example.

10
00:00:45.860 --> 00:00:49.320
Log it.

11
00:00:49.320 --> 00:00:56.320
Parts taken from the store are issued here, and their cost is added to the job.

12
00:00:56.320 --> 00:01:01.070
When the work is done, set it to Resolved.

13
00:01:01.070 --> 00:01:09.300
Say what was done. The tenant who reported it sees this note.

14
00:01:09.300 --> 00:01:15.530
Update. The job is closed, with its full history, costs and times.
